lisa-design:
- Candidates in one global order (priority desc, RuleSet, rule); final stops everything after it and fails closed (a final rule whose where passed suppresses lower rules even if its actions fail).
- Dedupe on firing via fired[rule]; a failing/erroring where doesn't consume it.
- Each rule's actions stage against an overlay and commit all-or-nothing; a set applies only with an allowed verdict; one Set intent per key.
- ActionIntent is a tagged struct (readable goldens, FakeRails matching); requestApproval -> Unsupported without consulting rails.
- now = injected Clock, else the event time (deterministic replays); run/approval come from event.data.facts on factory.* events.
- PoC rule fixes: review-whole-stack priority 50; announce-ptbr-live guarded with has(); release-docs items bound to params.trainManifest via item.state.manifest.

